.TH tudocx n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tudocx
.PP
Minimal Word (\fB.docx\fR, Office Open XML) helpers in pure Tcl.
.PP
\fBtudocx\fR writes simple paragraph documents and reads the text of any Word document back. It is the counterpart of \fBtuodf\fR for Office Open XML and not a Word toolkit: no styles, tables, images or numbering when writing.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tudocx 0.1
.CE
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tudocx::createText docxFile paragraphs ?-title T? ?-creator C?
::tclutils::tudocx::paragraphs docxFile
::tclutils::tudocx::text docxFile
::tclutils::tudocx::part docxFile name
::tclutils::tudocx::parts docxFile
.CE
.IP \(bu
\fBcreateText\fR writes \fB[Content_Types].xml\fR, \fB_rels/.rels\fR, \fBword/document.xml\fR and \fBdocProps/core.xml\fR / \fBapp.xml\fR. In a paragraph a tab becomes \fBw:tab\fR, a newline \fBw:br\fR. \fB\-title\fR and \fB\-creator\fR go into \fBdocProps/core.xml\fR. Returns the file name.
.IP \(bu
\fBparagraphs\fR returns the text of every paragraph of the main document part (found through \fB_rels/.rels\fR, usually \fBword/document.xml\fR) in document order: headings, list items and table cells included. \fBw:tab\fR is \fB\et\fR, \fBw:br\fR is \fB\en\fR. Deleted text of tracked changes (\fBw:delText\fR) and field codes (\fBw:instrText\fR) are left out. Headers, footers, footnotes and comments are in other parts and are not read.
.IP \(bu
\fBtext\fR joins the paragraphs with \fB\en\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBpart\fR returns one container part as text (UTF\-8), \fBparts\fR the member names.
.PP
Errors: \fB{TCLUTILS TUDOCX PART name}\fR when there is no main document part; \fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION ...}\fR for bad options. A missing or damaged ZIP is reported by \fBtuzip\fR.
.SS Example
.CS
package require tclutils::tudocx

::tclutils::tudocx::createText demo.docx \
    {{First paragraph} {Second with \u00e4\u00f6\u00fc\u00df} {} "a\tb"} \
    -title Demo -creator Tcl
puts [::tclutils::tudocx::text demo.docx]
.CE
.SS Notes
.PP
Output is deterministic: a fixed timestamp for all entries, no dates in \fBdocProps/core.xml\fR. Word, LibreOffice and python\-docx open the files.
.PP
The reader is a small text extractor with regular expressions, not an XML parser. Command line: \fBbin/tudocx.tcl text|parts|create\fR.
